213","name":"ConditionallyCompletePartialOrderInf.toInfSet","meaning":"Extracts set infima.","effect_on_target":"Provides gauge sInf.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D214","name":"ENNReal.instCompleteLinearOrder","meaning":"Complete linear order on ENNReal.","effect_on_target":"Ensures gauge infima exist.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D215","name":"Iff","meaning":"Logical equivalence.","effect_on_target":"States zero characterizations.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D216","name":"InfSet.sInf","meaning":"Set infimum.","effect_on_target":"Computes the gauge.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D217","name":"AddCommMonoidWithOne.toAddMonoidWithOne","meaning":"Forgets additive commutativity.","effect_on_target":"Numeral-one infrastructure.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D218","name":"AddMonoidWithOne.toOne","meaning":"Extracts one.","effect_on_target":"Provides the modular bound 1.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D219","name":"One.toOfNat1","meaning":"Interprets numeral 1 as one.","effect_on_target":"States modular≤1.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D220","name":"instAddCommMonoidWithOneENNReal","meaning":"Standard addition and one on ENNReal.","effect_on_target":"Provides ENNReal 1.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D221","name":"DivInvMonoid.toDiv","meaning":"Extracts division.","effect_on_target":"Provides real division.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D222","name":"HDiv.hDiv","meaning":"Generic heterogeneous division.","effect_on_target":"Forms |X|/t.toReal.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D223","name":"MeasureTheory.lintegral","meaning":"Extended nonnegative Lebesgue integral.","effect_on_target":"Computes the modular.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D224","name":"Real.instDivInvMonoid","meaning":"Standard real division and inversion.","effect_on_target":"Divides by the scale.","status":"understood"},{"id":"D225","name":"instHDiv","meaning":"Lifts homogeneous division to HDiv.","effect_on_target":"Interprets the integrand quotient.","status":"understood"}],"translation":{"binders":["A type Ω with a measurable-space structure.","A probability measure μ on Ω.","An admissible ψ : ℝ→ℝ."],"hypotheses":["ψ is nonnegative, convex, and monotone on [0,∞).","ψ(0)=0 and ψ(x)→∞ as x→∞.","μ has total mass one."],"conclusions":["The finite-gauge AEEqFun subtype has a compatible real normed-space structure.","Its gauge-norm uniform space is complete, hence it is a real Banach space."],"mathematical_definitions":["ρψ,μ(X,t)=∫ ENNReal.ofReal(ψ(|X(ω)|/t.toReal)) dμ.","A scale t is admissible iff t≠0, t≠∞, and ρψ,μ(X,t)≤1.","The gauge is the ENNReal infimum of admissible scales.","For AEEqFun X, the gauge is evaluated on X.cast.","The space is {X | gauge(X)<∞}, with norm gauge(X).toReal and inherited pointwise operations."],"proposition_plain_english":"For every probability space and every nonnegative, convex, nondecreasing ψ on [0,∞) with ψ(0)=0 and ψ tending to infinity, the almost-everywhere classes of almost-everywhere strongly measurable real functions having finite Luxemburg-type gauge form a complete normed real vector space."},"restrictions_and_vacuity_risks":["Only probability measures are covered.","Elements are AEEqFun classes, not arbitrary functions.","Only finite-gauge classes belong to the space.","Scales explicitly exclude 0 and ∞.","An empty admissible-scale set has ENNReal infimum ∞ and gives no carrier element.","ψ is unconstrained on negative inputs, which the absolute value prevents sampling.","ofReal truncates negatives, but ψ is nonnegative on sampled inputs.","The conclusion asserts existence of structures, not their uniqueness.","NormedSpace and CompleteSpace existence are separate conjuncts over the same fixed norm/uniformity.","Zero belongs to the carrier, so the space is nonempty.","No separability, reflexivity, or duality property is asserted."],"ambiguities":["The dossier does not separately state that the modular computed from X.cast agrees with every a.e.-equal representative.","LocalDef004 is exposed through its constructor conditions rather than a complete printed inductive declaration."]}
